// SECOND DRAFT (M5): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
Skögul is at the table before you, rolling a dead man onto his face with the toe of her boot.
There is a deep, clean cut between his shoulder blades.
"New decree came down in the night." # speaker: skogul
She holds up a strip of birch bark, cut in a very small, very neat hand. The quartermaster's.
"A wound in the back means they ran, and Odin won't feed a man who ran. The fled go to Hel." # speaker: skogul
"So now you turn them over. Every time you're not sure. It costs a breath of daylight each time, so don't do it for fun." # speaker: skogul
She rolls the dead man back with the same boot, not unkindly, and waves him down the path.
"He told me he'd been standing on a hill with the sun behind him. Heroic. Also a lie." # speaker: skogul
* ["What about the ones who were ambushed?"]
  "Unlucky." # speaker: skogul
  "If you want to argue it with Odin, he takes letters. He doesn't read them, but he takes them." # speaker: skogul
* ["Understood."]
  "You'll get so you can see it before you turn them. Cowards stand very straight when they're dead. They've had practice." # speaker: skogul
  # fx: standing odin +1
- She hands you the bark. You read it twice. It says exactly what she said, with more words.
Down the queue, a big man in a good cloak is trying very hard not to let anyone see his back.
-> END
